// A grammar that names `eos`: its input is a sequence of segments, the arguments of a
// command line here, and each ends where `eos` stands. At a boundary there is no
// character, so `any*` and the until idioms stop at the end of their segment; what is
// published takes a list or a sequence of strings and nothing else.
//
// Its neighbour Segmented.gram.g.cs is what the emitter is expected to make of it: the
// forms over text private and under names of their own, the forms over segments that
// read through them, and the scans that stop at the end of a segment as well as where
// a delimiter begins.

Args    = items: Arg* & eof
Arg     = ("--output" | "-o") & eos & output: Value & eos
        | "--comment" & eos & comment: Comment & eos
        | "--quoted" & eos & quoted: Std.Quoted('\'') & eos
        | plain: Value & eos

Value   = any*
Comment = "/*" & (?!"*/" & any)* & "*/"

parse Args
